FIX SET-WORLD-MATRIX STRIDE: FE menus drew black — matrix copy scaled x4 by int typing

Set_World_Matrix @0x42020c copies a 3x3 SHORT matrix into world_matrix
@0x462fa4 (asm 0x420235: mov %cx,0x462fa4(%eax), eax = row*6+col*2 = short
stride). The int-typed world_matrix symbol made the decompiled
(&world_matrix)[i*3+j] scale the destination index x4: elements landed at
byte offsets 0/4/8/..., producing a garbled identity (m22=0, m33 written past
the matrix) for the front-end slab camera. Every FE text/screen quad is GTE-
transformed through this matrix (FUN_00422a6c __vr uploads), so all glyph
quads degenerated to zero height (measured: every vertex y=240) and the whole
front end rendered black. MEASURED root chain: FE text records byte-identical
to the sound-enabled wine reference at the title screen, but ref quad
(206,396..418, tpage 0x8b8) vs ours (flat y=240) with ref world matrix =
clean identity vs ours shifted. Pointer-scaling class (like DAT_00466a96,
patch 655-era table cases).

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -11944,7 +11944,13 @@
     iVar2 = 0;
     do {
       iVar3 = iVar2 + 1;
-      (&world_matrix)[iVar1 * 3 + iVar2] = *(undefined2 *)(param_1 + iVar1 * 6 + iVar2 * 2);
+      /* asm 0x420235: mov %cx,0x462fa4(%eax) with eax = row*6+col*2 -- a WORD store at SHORT
+         stride. world_matrix is int-typed, so Ghidra's (&world_matrix)[i*3+j] scaled the index
+         x4: the copied matrix landed at byte offsets 0/4/8/... instead of 0/2/4/... -> the FE
+         slab camera got a garbled identity (m22=0, m33 written past the matrix at +0x20) ->
+         every GTE-transformed front-end text/screen quad degenerated (flat y) -> BLACK menus. */
+      *(short *)((char *)&world_matrix + (iVar1 * 3 + iVar2) * 2) =
+           *(undefined2 *)(param_1 + iVar1 * 6 + iVar2 * 2);
       iVar2 = iVar3;
     } while (iVar3 < 3);
     iVar1 = iVar1 + 1;
